  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 332 AM EDT Mon Jul 6 2026\n\nThe long term forecast remains relatively unchanged with continued \nhot temperatures and daily chances for rain.\n\nBroad troughing will be the main feature through the period with an \nupper low sitting over the Ohio and Tennessee Valleys through at \nleast mid-week, then the upper level flow opens up to allow a few \ndisturbances to move over the area late week into the weekend. \nChances for isolated or scattered storms remains over at least some \nportion of the area each day this week but vary from day to day. \nSlightly drier conditions are now favored Wednesday and Thursday \nwhile PoPs generally remain around 20-35% Tuesday and Friday. An \nuptick in rain chances is seen for the weekend through guidance does \nshow some spread in the overall pattern this far out. \n\nHigh temperatures will be slightly above seasonable values with heat \nindex values in the upper 90s to low 100s each day. Some locations, \nparticularly in the southeast portion of the area, may still \napproach or exceed heat advisory criteria this week. Continue to \npractice heat safety!",
